+# Deploying the USDC Tip Jar to IPFS
+
+The site ships as a **static export** — plain HTML, JS and CSS served by IPFS gateways. Nothing runs server-side, so every route has to exist as a file and every environment value has to be baked in at build time.
+
+> **Nothing here has been uploaded.** This document is the runbook; the commands below are what actually publishes the site.
+
+---
+
+## What the production build config does
+
+`packages/nextjs/next.config.ts`, when `NEXT_PUBLIC_IPFS_BUILD=true`:
+
+| Setting | Why |
+|---|---|
+| `output: "export"` | Emits static HTML instead of a server build. |
+| `trailingSlash: true` | Emits `debug/index.html`, not `debug.html`. Gateways resolve a directory to its `index.html` but will not resolve a bare filename, so without this every route except `/` 404s. |
+| `images: { unoptimized: true }` | There is no image optimizer behind a gateway. |
+| Fails if `NEXT_PUBLIC_PRODUCTION_URL` is unset | Otherwise `og:image` and canonical URLs bake in `http://localhost:3000` and nothing warns you until someone shares the link. |
+
+`yarn build:ipfs` (in `packages/nextjs/package.json`) wraps that up: it cleans `.next`/`out` first, sets `NEXT_PUBLIC_TARGET_NETWORK=base` so the app targets Base 8453 instead of the local fork, and loads the `localStorage` polyfill through `NODE_OPTIONS` so Node 25's broken Web Storage global does not crash the prerender workers (see README).
+
+---
+
+## 1. Preflight
+
+### Deploy the contract to Base
+
+The static bundle needs a TipJar address for chain 8453 in `deployedContracts.ts`. Until you deploy, the site builds fine but renders "No TipJar found on Base".
+
+```bash
+yarn generate                # create a deployer keystore, once
+yarn account                 # fund the printed address with a little ETH on Base
+yarn deploy --network base   # writes the 8453 entry into deployedContracts.ts
+```
+
+Source verification on Basescan is optional and needs an `[etherscan]` entry for `base` in `packages/foundry/foundry.toml` plus an API key; see the [SE-2 deployment docs](https://docs.scaffoldeth.io/deploying/deploy-smart-contracts).
+
+Confirm it landed:
+
+```bash
+grep -A2 '8453: {' packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts
+```
+
+### Pick the domain
+
+The ENS name decides `NEXT_PUBLIC_PRODUCTION_URL`. For `tipjar.yourname.eth` the gateway URL is `https://tipjar.yourname.eth.link`, and `https://tipjar.yourname.eth.limo` resolves the same content hash. Pick one and use it consistently — the URL is baked into the build, so switching later means a rebuild and a new CID.
+
+### Set the RPC
+
+`https://mainnet.base.org` rate-limits hard and is not acceptable for a public site. Get an Alchemy (or similar) Base endpoint and pass it as `NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_RPC_URL`; `scaffold.config.ts` turns it into an `rpcOverrides` entry for chain 8453.
+
+Also set your own `NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_CONNECT_PROJECT_ID` from [cloud.reown.com](https://cloud.reown.com) — the scaffold default is shared by every SE-2 project.
+
+### Check the social card
+
+`packages/nextjs/public/thumbnail.png` is the 1200×630 unfurl image. Replace it if the branding changed; `getMetadata` resolves it against `NEXT_PUBLIC_PRODUCTION_URL`.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Build
+
+```bash
+cd packages/nextjs
+
+NEXT_PUBLIC_PRODUCTION_URL="https://tipjar.yourname.eth.link" \
+NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_RPC_URL="https://base-mainnet.g.alchemy.com/v2/<key>" \
+NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY="<key>" \
+NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_CONNECT_PROJECT_ID="<project-id>" \
+  yarn build:ipfs
+```
+
+`build:ipfs` already runs `yarn clean` (deleting `.next` and `out`) and `yarn lint`. Never skip the clean — uploading a stale `out/` is the single most common way to "deploy" a change that never shipped.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Verify the bundle before uploading
+
+```bash
+cd packages/nextjs
+
+# Every route exists as a directory with an index.html
+ls out/index.html out/*/index.html
+
+# og:image is absolute and on the production domain — not localhost
+grep -o '<meta property="og:image"[^>]*>' out/index.html
+
+# The app targets Base, not the local fork
+grep -o 'Tips in USDC on.\{0,40\}' out/index.html     # expect "Base"
+
+# Your Base RPC made it into the bundle (substitute your own host)
+grep -rl "base-mainnet.g.alchemy.com" out/_next/static/chunks/ | head -1
+
+# The build is newer than the source it came from
+stat -c '%y %n' app/page.tsx out/
+```
+
+`mainnet.base.org` will still appear in the bundle — viem's own `base` chain definition carries it as a last-resort fallback. What matters is that your endpoint is there and, per `wagmiConfig`, tried first.
+
+If a change you made is missing, `grep` the export for a string you added — that tells you whether the build picked it up or you are looking at the wrong directory:
+
+```bash
+grep -rl "some new string" out/_next/static/chunks/
+```
+
+Serve it locally exactly as a gateway would, and click through:
+
+```bash
+python3 -m http.server 8099 --directory out
+# then check http://127.0.0.1:8099/ , /debug/ , /blockexplorer/
+for path in / /debug/ /blockexplorer/; do
+  echo "$path -> $(curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' -L http://127.0.0.1:8099$path)"
+done
+```
+
+Walk the real flow in a browser before uploading: connect a wallet on the wrong chain and confirm the switch prompt, then approve, tip, and reject a transaction to confirm the UI recovers.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Upload
+
+```bash
+cd packages/nextjs
+yarn bgipfs upload config init -u https://upload.bgipfs.com
+yarn bgipfs upload out
+```
+
+Save the CID.
+
+`yarn ipfs` does the build and the upload in one step, but it calls `build:ipfs` underneath, so it needs the same environment prefix as step 2 — without `NEXT_PUBLIC_PRODUCTION_URL` it stops at the config guard:
+
+```bash
+NEXT_PUBLIC_PRODUCTION_URL="https://tipjar.yourname.eth.link" \
+NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_RPC_URL="https://base-mainnet.g.alchemy.com/v2/<key>" \
+  yarn ipfs
+```
+
+Share for review before touching ENS:
+
+```
+https://community.bgipfs.com/ipfs/<CID>
+```
+
+A CID that is unchanged from the last deploy means the uploaded bytes were identical — either the build did not pick up your change or you handed the uploader the wrong directory. The `grep` in step 3 tells you which.
+
+---
+
+## 5. Verify the deployed CID
+
+```bash
+CID=<your-cid>
+GATEWAY=https://community.bgipfs.com
+
+for path in / /debug/ /blockexplorer/; do
+  echo "$path -> $(curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' -L "$GATEWAY/ipfs/$CID$path")"
+done
+
+curl -s -L "$GATEWAY/ipfs/$CID/" | grep -E 'og:image|<title>'
+```
+
+All 200s, and the metadata pointing at your production domain rather than localhost.
+
+---
+
+## 6. Point ENS at it
+
+Two mainnet transactions, gas required.
+
+**First deploy only — create the subname:**
+
+1. Open `https://app.ens.domains/yourname.eth`
+2. **Subnames → New subname**, enter `tipjar`, skip the profile, confirm in your wallet.
+
+**Every deploy — set the content hash:**
+
+1. Open `https://app.ens.domains/tipjar.yourname.eth`
+2. **Records → Edit Records → Other**
+3. Set the content hash to `ipfs://<CID>` and confirm.
+
+Only set the content hash after the CID above has been reviewed.
+
+---
+
+## 7. Verify live
+
+```bash
+NAME=tipjar.yourname.eth
+
+# The content hash on chain
+RESOLVER=$(cast call 0x00000000000C2e074eC69A0dFb2997BA6C7d2e1e \
+  "resolver(bytes32)(address)" $(cast namehash $NAME) --rpc-url https://eth.llamarpc.com)
+cast call $RESOLVER "contenthash(bytes32)(bytes)" $(cast namehash $NAME) \
+  --rpc-url https://eth.llamarpc.com
+
+# The gateway (allow 5-15 minutes for caches)
+curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" -L "https://$NAME.link"
+curl -s -L "https://$NAME.link" | grep 'og:image'
+curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" -L "https://$NAME.link/debug/"
+```
+
+---
+
+## Redeploying
+
+Every code change: `yarn build:ipfs` (which cleans first) → re-verify step 3 → upload → confirm the CID changed → update the ENS content hash. The subname already exists, so only the second ENS transaction is needed.
+
+---
+
+## Known limits of the static build
+
+- **The tip feed reads logs directly, and this is the first thing that will break.** `useScaffoldEventHistory` is marked deprecated for production in SE-2 itself, and logs a warning on every non-local chain. It paginates `getLogs` in 500-block batches from the deployment block to head — Base mines ~43,200 blocks/day, so that is roughly 86 sequential round trips per day of jar history **on every page load**, plus one `getBlock` per event for timestamps. It is fine for a fresh jar on a paid RPC and untenable a few months in; the live-polling query also fails silently, since the error state on the feed only covers the historical fetch. Move the feed to an indexer before the jar has any real history — `.agents/skills/ponder/SKILL.md` and `.agents/skills/subgraph/SKILL.md` both cover it, and `TipJar` already emits everything an indexer needs.
+- **Block explorer address and transaction pages are prerendered for the zero address only.** Static export cannot generate a page per address. The main explorer page works; the sub-pages are a local development tool and 404 on a gateway.
+- **Environment values are frozen at build time.** Changing the RPC or the production URL means a rebuild, a new CID and a new ENS transaction.
